ui/accessibility: map NSAccessibilityIndexForChildUIElementParameterizedAttribute on macOS 26.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
When the host deployment target is macOS 26 the private fallback macros are
skipped, but the macOS 26 SDK spells this constant
NSAccessibilityIndexForChildUIElementAttribute (no "Parameterized"), so
browser_accessibility_cocoa.mm fails with an undeclared identifier on the
host toolchain. Alias the old name to the SDK constant in that case.

--- a/ui/accessibility/platform/ax_private_attributes_mac.h	2026-10-28 02:54:23.652317525 +0300
+++ b/ui/accessibility/platform/ax_private_attributes_mac.h	2026-10-28 02:54:23.656675547 +0300
@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@
 #define NSAccessibilityUIElementsForSearchPredicateParameterizedAttribute \
   @"AXUIElementsForSearchPredicate"
 #define NSAccessibilityVisitedAttribute @"AXVisited"
+#elif !defined(NSAccessibilityIndexForChildUIElementParameterizedAttribute)
+// EmberBSD: the macOS 26 SDK names this constant without "Parameterized".
+#define NSAccessibilityIndexForChildUIElementParameterizedAttribute \
+  NSAccessibilityIndexForChildUIElementAttribute
 #endif
 
 // Accessibility attributes not found in the SDK.
